messages:
anya_prod_design: quick PSA after yesterday's usability session — compact model rows have multiple a11y nits we should triage: focus flicker on dark theme, skiplink landing under sticky header, and extra tab stops inside empty cells.

sam_ui_eng: thanks — I noticed the flicker when I tab through really fast. It looks like we draw a focus outline and also animate a subtle shadow which lags. Could be browser repaint.

dina_a11y: repro steps: Console > Models > Compact view > Tab through with keyboard; on Chrome + mac I can see a faint duplicate focus ring on the previous row for a split second. VoiceOver on mac sometimes vocalizes the previous row first then the current row (order gets noisy).

mohit_pm: which of these are regressions vs intended style? Need estimate to decide ship window.

sam_ui_eng: style was added for mouse hover emphasis, not specifically keyboard. We accidentally applied the same transform/box-shadow on :focus. I'll scope the hover animation to :hover only and remove transform for :focus.

Dina_a11y: recommended fixes: 1) do not animate transform/box-shadow on keyboard focus, 2) use a solid 3px focus ring for keyboard with contrast >= 4.5:1 for small targets, 3) ensure only the row container has tabindex=0, not individual cells, 4) fix skiplink target scroll offset.

sam_ui_eng: proposed CSS patch:
```css
/* keyboard-first focus */
.row:focus {
  transform: none !important;
  box-shadow: none !important;
  outline: 3px solid var(--focus-accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
.row:hover { /* keep hover affordance */
  transform: scale(1.01);
  box-shadow: var(--hover-elevation);
}
/* skiplink target anchor should account for sticky header */
[target=".models-list"]:target {
  scroll-margin-top: var(--sticky-header-height);
}
```

anya_prod_design: nice. Also a copy/announce nit: when a model row status flips to "training" we sync a live badge but there's no SR announcement. Can we add aria-live on the status node so SR users hear the transition?

dina_a11y: yes add `role="status" aria-live="polite"` to non-critical status text, and `aria-live="assertive"` only if it's an error. For the training badge polite is fine. Also ensure the status element has an accessible name (e.g., "Status: training") via visually-hidden label or accessible text.

mohit_pm: prioritization? this sounds like low-sev visual + medium for SR announcements.

dina_a11y: fix order: 1) remove focus animations that cause flicker (small PR), 2) audit tabindex + remove redundant focusable cells (small PR), 3) skiplink scroll-margin fix + add Lighthouse test (medium), 4) aria-live + accessible name for status (small). I can draft QA steps and run VoiceOver/NVDA checks.

sam_ui_eng: I'll do 1+2 today and open PR. For 3 I need to confirm the CSS variable for sticky header height works across responsive breakpoints — might be a tiny layout tweak.

access_bot: accessibility-checker: created ticket A11Y-202 — Compact rows: focus repaint, tabindex duplication, skiplink offset, and aria-live for status. Suggested CI checks: keyboard tab-order test, axe CI for focusable elements, and a contrast lint for focus ring colors.

anya_prod_design: also add an example in the docs about keyboard-first interactions for dense tables — remind designers not to use transforms for keyboard focus.

dina_a11y: QA script I'll add to the checklist: 1) Keyboard only: Tab/Shift-Tab across first 20 rows, ensure single focus ring and correct SR announcement; 2) VoiceOver/NVDA: confirm row focus announces "Model name, Status: X" once; 3) Skiplink: activate skiplink and verify the first row is visible under sticky header; 4) Empty cells: ensure they are skipped in tab order.

sam_ui_eng: makes sense. I'll tag you on the PR for review. Expect a small visual diff + unit test simulating tab order in jest-dom.

mohit_pm: timeline for release? if small PRs land today we can include in next patch. Otherwise schedule for next sprint.

dina_a11y: I'll start the SR passes as soon as PR lands. If VoiceOver/NVDA show surprises we'll escalate.

anya_prod_design: thanks all — this is a good cleanup before we flip Compact view to default for power users. :sparkles:  "
